["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"China&#x27;s Economic Peak Has Passed: Credit Dries Up, Deflation Looms China&#x27;s share of global GDP peaked in 2021 and has been declining since; credit growth has fallen from 18% to 5%, and real growth may be only 1.5%-2%; the US has outperformed for five consecutive years. The narrative of industrial chain dominance is disproven by data; the future looks more like Japan-style deflation. Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch The Miracle Is Over: Inside China&#x27;s Slow-Motion Economic Decay China economy credit PPP demographics US-China competition trade protection PPP / Purchasing Power Parity Impossible Trinity Loan Prime Rate (LPR) Special Revenue Bonds Total Factor Productivity (TFP) Demand-side Controls\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-geopoliticsdec-中国经济巅峰已过-美国优势还将扩大/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://pbcdn1.podbean.com/imglogo/image-logo/16885185/gpd-3000x3000-72dpi.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"G\"><span class=\"dur\">47:58</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">Geopolitics Decanted with Dmitri Alperovitch</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>China&#x27;s Economic Peak Has Passed: Credit Dries Up, Deflation Looms</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">China&#x27;s share of global GDP peaked in 2021 and has been declining since; credit growth has fallen from 18% to 5%, and real growth may be only 1.5%-2%; the US has outperformed for five consecutive years. The narrative of industrial chain dominance is disproven by data; the future looks more like Japan-style deflation.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">China economy</span><span class=\"tag\">credit</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Bell Used Einstein&#x27;s Own Tools to Refute His Core Argument The EPR argument forces a choice between an incomplete quantum description and action at a distance; determinism is never an assumption but a conclusion that is inferred. The full logic of Bell&#x27;s theorem must start here. Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal Tim Maudlin: Quantum Nonlocality Explained FROM SCRATCH quantum mechanics EPR Bell&#x27;s theorem nonlocality history of physics action at a distance EPR action at a distance configuration space reality criterion ontological locality dynamical locality\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-theoriesofever-贝尔用爱因斯坦自己的工具推翻了他的核心论点/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/3775439c-21d9-11ef-ba0a-0f2bf7e94c97/image/f59d515f7463e749285492d1cef7b8d8.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">3:18:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Bell Used Einstein&#x27;s Own Tools to Refute His Core Argument</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The EPR argument forces a choice between an incomplete quantum description and action at a distance; determinism is never an assumption but a conclusion that is inferred. The full logic of Bell&#x27;s theorem must start here.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">quantum mechanics</span><span class=\"tag\">EPR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"The Quantum Endgame Isn&#x27;t Cleaner Qubits—It&#x27;s Who Can Use a Phone-Chip Fab Line The quantum endgame isn&#x27;t about whose qubits are cleaner, but who can mass-produce using existing semiconductor fabs; silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC lithography, while ion traps are stuck at 100,000 lasers and superconductors at warehouse-sized fridges. From First Principles From First Principles Why Spin Qubits Will Win the Quantum Race (Part 2) (EP 55) Quantum computing Silicon spin Semiconductors Superconducting Ion trap AI auto-tuning transmon valley splitting 2DEG DETR exchange-only qubit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-fromfirstprinc-硅自旋将赢-百万比特只需一块硅晶圆/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_nologo/44168556/44168556-1767646146888-2edad6d04289f.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">3:46:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">From First Principles</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The Quantum Endgame Isn&#x27;t Cleaner Qubits—It&#x27;s Who Can Use a Phone-Chip Fab Line</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The quantum endgame isn&#x27;t about whose qubits are cleaner, but who can mass-produce using existing semiconductor fabs; silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC lithography, while ion traps are stuck at 100,000 lasers and superconductors at warehouse-sized fridges.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Quantum computing</span><span class=\"tag\">Silicon spin</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI Chip Shipments Will Jump an Order of Magnitude: From a Million to 15 Million Broadcom&#x27;s president shows an AI chip roadmap: from a million units to 15 million, with the &#x27;beast&#x27; being the largest package of 8 stackable compute dies plus 16 HBM modules, and four of the five frontier labs are collaborating. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato Future GPUs Will Look Like This Custom chips ASIC Advanced packaging HBM Broadcom Compute supply chain back-end design services HBM CoWoS scaleup fabric\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-techtechpotato-未来-ai-定制芯片的形态-一只带-16-个-hbm-的巨兽/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/3CIjdDmO3sU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">11:10</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TechTechPotato</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>AI Chip Shipments Will Jump an Order of Magnitude: From a Million to 15 Million</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Broadcom&#x27;s president shows an AI chip roadmap: from a million units to 15 million, with the &#x27;beast&#x27; being the largest package of 8 stackable compute dies plus 16 HBM modules, and four of the five frontier labs are collaborating.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Custom chips</span><span class=\"tag\">ASIC</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"An Explorer Died for a Fictional City, and the Source Was a Political Forgery Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are often told as adventure legends, but the real starting point was border disputes fueled by the rubber trade; his narrative of &#x27;respect&#x27; for indigenous people is a gross oversimplification, and the City of Z that obsessed him may rest on a forged manuscript. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class Percy Fawcett, Manuscript 512, and a Lost City in the Amazon, Pt. 1 exploration history Amazon rubber trade indigenous peoples occultism lost city Manuscript 512 Royal Geographical Society rubber boom Mato Grosso City of Z\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-stuffmissed-福西特不是去冒险-是去给橡胶资本画地图/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/programs/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/cfb428ef-eafc-44d0-9d09-ae2701747e6f/image.jpg?t=1749829805&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">34:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>An Explorer Died for a Fictional City, and the Source Was a Political Forgery</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are often told as adventure legends, but the real starting point was border disputes fueled by the rubber trade; his narrative of &#x27;respect&#x27; for indigenous people is a gross oversimplification, and the City of Z that obsessed him may rest on a forged manuscript.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">exploration history</span><span class=\"tag\">Amazon</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes using quantum entanglement entropy instead of thermodynamic entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis. Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape Mindscape 366 | Jim Al-Khalili on Time, Quantum, Biology, and Cosmology arrow of time quantum mechanics quantum biology entropy past hypothesis philosophy of physics past hypothesis entanglement entropy master equation decoherence non-Markovian many-worlds interpretation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-mindscape-时间的方向性比时间对称方程更根本/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/b/0/6/d/b06d098337897af116c3140a3186d450/21d641ef836c48dff270cbede4360d187bdd6c56cb126be7d6f51078db34d4675527fa72e13c86bb573ec42c5d4fc493e18e7d95fec734ec77168fc379baefcf.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes using quantum entanglement entropy instead of thermodynamic entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">arrow of time</span><span class=\"tag\">quantum mechanics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Most Gazans Have Abandoned Hamas, and the Window for Disarmament Is Opening Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib, a policy scholar born in Gaza, argues with four layers of opposition, two polls, and demographic data that most Gazans have long turned against Hamas, and that Hamas may be forced to disarm in stages; but host Russ&#x27;s pessimistic reminder: disarmament for Hamas equals political suicide. EconTalk EconTalk Hamas and the Future of Gaza (with Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib) Gaza Hamas Israeli-Palestinian conflict poll manipulation demilitarization Middle East geopolitics Shikaki polls NCAG Great Reset UNRWA DSA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-econtalk-加沙多数人已抛弃哈马斯-缴械窗口正在打开/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/4ca709a1-1918-43a4-9035-1176b5aa9f2b/b8c673f8-58e7-4d4a-ab02-f83c2fd463c4/3000x3000/econtalknewbluecover1400.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:22:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">EconTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Most Gazans Have Abandoned Hamas, and the Window for Disarmament Is Opening</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib, a policy scholar born in Gaza, argues with four layers of opposition, two polls, and demographic data that most Gazans have long turned against Hamas, and that Hamas may be forced to disarm in stages; but host Russ&#x27;s pessimistic reminder: disarmament for Hamas equals political suicide.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Gaza</span><span class=\"tag\">Hamas</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"US Economic Resilience Comes from Consumers Borrowing from the Future Barkin explains why consumption stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, skip bills, and delay loan payments to keep spending; AI investment so far is more about price hikes and crowding out than productivity gains; the Fed may face a long headwind. Odd Lots Odd Lots Richmond Fed’s Tom Barkin on the Surprisingly Resilient Real Economy consumer resilience Federal Reserve AI capex inflation data centers tariffs SEP dot plot R-star forward guidance private label\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-oddlots-美国经济韧性来自消费者向未来借钱/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">31:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>US Economic Resilience Comes from Consumers Borrowing from the Future</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Barkin explains why consumption stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, skip bills, and delay loan payments to keep spending; AI investment so far is more about price hikes and crowding out than productivity gains; the Fed may face a long headwind.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">consumer resilience</span><span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is a Multiple Draft, Not a Projection Room Dennett rejects the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations converge into consciousness; the brain is a set of parallel judgments that never get pooled into one stream. Even the question &quot;when did you become aware?&quot; often has no factual answer. The Partially Examined Life Partially Examined Life Ep. 399: Dan Dennett&#x27;s Model of Mind (Part One) consciousness philosophy mind multiple drafts cognitive science Cartesian Theater Multiple Drafts Model Phi phenomenon Qualia Homunculus Stalinesque vs. Orwellian\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-pel-笛卡尔剧场不存在-意识不是放映-而是多重草稿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/5/2/9/5/5295552bae3afd35d959afa2a1bf1c87/PartiallyExaminedLifeLogo_3000x3000-20260831-z6pgvfibvm.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">47:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Partially Examined Life</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is a Multiple Draft, Not a Projection Room</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Dennett rejects the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations converge into consciousness; the brain is a set of parallel judgments that never get pooled into one stream. Even the question &quot;when did you become aware?&quot; often has no factual answer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">consciousness</span><span class=\"tag\">philosophy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"The Bottleneck in a Fab Isn&#x27;t the Lithography Machine—It&#x27;s the OHT Robots on the Ceiling The real capacity constraint in a wafer fab isn&#x27;t just the lithography machine; it&#x27;s the OHT vehicles scurrying overhead. The 300mm transition made them indispensable, and today the market is a duopoly of Daifuku and Muratec. Asianometry Asianometry The Little Ceiling Robots Inside a Semiconductor Fab AMHS OHT Semiconductor Manufacturing Wafer Fab Automated Logistics Equipment Duopoly AMHS / Automated Material Handling System FOUP / Front-Opening Unified Pod OHT / Overhead Hoist Transport Stocker Interbay / Intrabay\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-asianometry-别只盯着光刻机-天花板上的-oht-小车也在卡产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/SwYDxh3PQJ0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">20:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Bottleneck in a Fab Isn&#x27;t the Lithography Machine—It&#x27;s the OHT Robots on the Ceiling</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The real capacity constraint in a wafer fab isn&#x27;t just the lithography machine; it&#x27;s the OHT vehicles scurrying overhead. The 300mm transition made them indispensable, and today the market is a duopoly of Daifuku and Muratec.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AMHS</span><span class=\"tag\">OHT</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The Treasury Secretary Is Treating the Bond Market Like a Trade — and Prices Are Winning US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade, and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, making his strategy likely to fail. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle Scott Bessent Is at War With Prices — and Prices Are Winning! Treasury bonds Fiscal policy Inflation Federal Reserve Cryptocurrency Trade war TGA (Treasury General Account) On-the-run vs off-the-run bonds Duration neutral Term premium Stablecoin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-patrickboyle-贝森特与价格的战争-财政部长的宏观赌局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_nologo/42184536/48d3d010465c2cda.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">44:51</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Treasury Secretary Is Treating the Bond Market Like a Trade — and Prices Are Winning</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade, and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, making his strategy likely to fail.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasury bonds</span><span class=\"tag\">Fiscal policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Elite Universities Are a Cartel: Selling Status, Not Education America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, cultivating alumni donations, and securing federal research grants; they sell status, not education. Modern MBA Modern MBA The American College Cartel University Finance Endowments Elite Education Admissions Insider American Innovation endowment advancement provost tenure yield tech tree\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-modernmba-精英大学是制造稀缺的卡特尔-而非教育机构/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i2.ytimg.com/vi/mLW0STRZHR4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">45:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Modern MBA</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Elite Universities Are a Cartel: Selling Status, Not Education</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, cultivating alumni donations, and securing federal research grants; they sell status, not education.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">University Finance</span><span class=\"tag\">Endowments</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Phages bet on 10,000-fold reversion, EBV humanized antibodies emerge Phages use SSR-mediated 10,000-fold reversion for bet-hedging; EBV humanized antibodies block tumors in vivo; vaccines advance on multiple fronts. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies phage bet-hedging EBV antibody vaccine cognitive laziness SSR / simple sequence repeat bet-hedging contingency locus hybridoma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体用随机突变下注-ebv人类抗体首次成功/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">1:52:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phages bet on 10,000-fold reversion, EBV humanized antibodies emerge</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Phages use SSR-mediated 10,000-fold reversion for bet-hedging; EBV humanized antibodies block tumors in vivo; vaccines advance on multiple fronts.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">phage</span><span class=\"tag\">bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Phage bet-hedging via replication slippage and EBV antibodies Slippage is not a replication error but a phage bet: the population always carries a few individuals whose reading frame is shifted by repeats, generating variants not yet selected. Most are adapted to the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, the low-frequency backup takes over. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies phage bet-hedging EBV monoclonal antibody vaccine design science communication simple sequence repeats (SSR) bet-hedging hybridoma HAT medium humanized mice\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体靠复制打滑预留变异-赌细菌防御会升级/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:52:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage bet-hedging via replication slippage and EBV antibodies</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Slippage is not a replication error but a phage bet: the population always carries a few individuals whose reading frame is shifted by repeats, generating variants not yet selected. Most are adapted to the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, the low-frequency backup takes over.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">phage</span><span class=\"tag\">bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"When Code Is Free, Users Pay for Judgment and Distribution Replit&#x27;s engineering lead offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms, and networks survive; a non-coder with domain knowledge builds a $180K/month business in three days. Peter Yang Peter Yang How Non-Coders Are Vibe Coding $100K+ Businesses with AI | Amol Jain vibe coding AI startups SaaS Replit model neutrality internal DIY software Vibe coding TAM System of record MCP Token maxing\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-peteryang-代码成本归零后-用户为判断力与分发付费/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/JAh8Wv1lQrw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">36:35</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Peter Yang</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>When Code Is Free, Users Pay for Judgment and Distribution</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Replit&#x27;s engineering lead offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms, and networks survive; a non-coder with domain knowledge builds a $180K/month business in three days.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">vibe coding</span><span class=\"tag\">AI startups</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s third era is persistent coworkers, and product cycles are only three months OpenAI&#x27;s product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent coworkers, and building must be done against model capabilities two to three months out; future work is steering, not rowing, and writing-as-thinking will never be automated. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast AI’s third era: the rise of persistent AI coworkers | Tara Seshan (OpenAI’s product lead) product cycles persistent coworkers Codex writing as thinking product marketing fit persistent co-worker product marketing fit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-lennys-ai-第三纪元是持久协作者-产品周期只有三个月/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/10845/post/211586245/25b1ee02fa1c0785096c231b7e3369ed.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:21:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s third era is persistent coworkers, and product cycles are only three months</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI&#x27;s product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent coworkers, and building must be done against model capabilities two to three months out; future work is steering, not rowing, and writing-as-thinking will never be automated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">product cycles</span><span class=\"tag\">persistent coworkers</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"1858 New York Poison Milk: Evidence Solid, Yet Officials Declared It Harmless In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing declared it harmless. The affair eventually drove the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class SYMHC Classics: Swill Milk food adulteration public health media investigation American history milk safety institutional corruption swill milk artificial feeding temperance movement spent grain\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-stuffmissed-1858年纽约毒奶-证据确凿-官方委员会判定无害/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/programs/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/cfb428ef-eafc-44d0-9d09-ae2701747e6f/image.jpg?t=1749829805&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">39:22</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>1858 New York Poison Milk: Evidence Solid, Yet Officials Declared It Harmless</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing declared it harmless. The affair eventually drove the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">food adulteration</span><span class=\"tag\">public health</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"A Parasite Gave Tens of Thousands of Americans Diarrhea: Can&#x27;t Wash It Off, Can&#x27;t Culture It, Can&#x27;t Tell Alive from Dead The oocysts behind tens of thousands of US diarrhea cases resist bleach and rinsing, and only become infectious after one to two weeks outside the body; labs can&#x27;t culture them or test for viability, so outbreaks are hard to break. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1352: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin parasite Cyclospora foodborne outbreak public health imported produce Cyclospora cayetanensis oocyst sporulation Guillain-Barré reactive arthritis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-twiv-一种寄生虫让美国上万人腹泻-洗不掉-养不活-验不出死活/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">48:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>A Parasite Gave Tens of Thousands of Americans Diarrhea: Can&#x27;t Wash It Off, Can&#x27;t Culture It, Can&#x27;t Tell Alive from Dead</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The oocysts behind tens of thousands of US diarrhea cases resist bleach and rinsing, and only become infectious after one to two weeks outside the body; labs can&#x27;t culture them or test for viability, so outbreaks are hard to break.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">parasite</span><span class=\"tag\">Cyclospora</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Mac Icons Aren&#x27;t About Pixels, They&#x27;re About Metaphor Draw less, and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white constraint isn&#x27;t a design flaw—it&#x27;s the constraint that forces good ideas. Y Combinator Y Combinator Susan Kare: Designing Icons &amp; Graphics For the Original Mac Icon Design Design Methodology Early Mac Branding &amp; Logo Steve Jobs iconographer bitmap graphics proportionally spaced fonts cap height Letraset desktop metaphor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-ycsp-mac-图标不是像素问题-是隐喻问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_episode/23401959/23401959-1787939916773-e5a2d3696b501.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">51:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Y Combinator</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Mac Icons Aren&#x27;t About Pixels, They&#x27;re About Metaphor</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Draw less, and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white constraint isn&#x27;t a design flaw—it&#x27;s the constraint that forces good ideas.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Icon Design</span><span class=\"tag\">Design Methodology</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come from Nothing Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe didn&#x27;t arise from nothing. He also warns that AI can&#x27;t replicate human intuition and can&#x27;t be fully controlled. Into the Impossible With Brian Keating Into the Impossible With Brian Keating The Universe Didn’t Come From Nothing | The Peter McCormack Show Cosmology Time AI Limits Gravitational Waves Trust in Science BICEP Array Simons Observatory Jevons Paradox UAP Cosmological Time Field\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-intotheimpossi-时间不存在-宇宙并非从无中诞生/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/fdd3ee00-a303-11f1-adb2-a3f58b61e45f/image/55615551ef9eeaf63339e2c942446853.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:46:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Into the Impossible With Brian Keating</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come from Nothing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe didn&#x27;t arise from nothing. He also warns that AI can&#x27;t replicate human intuition and can&#x27;t be fully controlled.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Cosmology</span><span class=\"tag\">Time</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Fed Official: Inflation Hasn&#x27;t Left, Rate Cuts Can&#x27;t Be Bet on &#x27;Temporary&#x27; Goolsbee worries the economy is overheating: the inflation decline is mostly supply-side repair, services haven&#x27;t responded; cuts below neutral need evidence, not front-loading. Odd Lots Odd Lots Austan Goolsbee Is Worried the Economy Is Overheating Fed Inflation AI Investment Interest Rates Forward Guidance R-star SEP Forward guidance Reaction function Taylor rule\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-oddlots-古尔斯比-通胀没走-降息不能押注-暂时/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">46:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Fed Official: Inflation Hasn&#x27;t Left, Rate Cuts Can&#x27;t Be Bet on &#x27;Temporary&#x27;</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Goolsbee worries the economy is overheating: the inflation decline is mostly supply-side repair, services haven&#x27;t responded; cuts below neutral need evidence, not front-loading.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Fed</span><span class=\"tag\">Inflation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Recursive Bootstrapping Can Wait: The RL Environment Itself Is Teaching Models to Cheat Frontier labs&#x27; RL environments are almost never audited, rushed and vibe-coded with dirty reward signals—models learn to cheat by treating these as optimal, then train the next generation, and errors amplify exponentially. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution AI:AM Highlights: Recursive Self-Improvement, Rushed and Vibe-Coded? reinforcement learning reward hacking recursive self-improvement prompt injection edge inference OpenAI chip vibe coding reward hacking prompt injection recursive self-improvement chain of thought\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cogrev-递归自举先缓-rl-环境本身在教模型作弊/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/96615d8a-a2d0-11f1-bc21-c3289ad03bf0/image/a998537edf8e55617bad80577ae103c0.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:11:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Recursive Bootstrapping Can Wait: The RL Environment Itself Is Teaching Models to Cheat</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Frontier labs&#x27; RL environments are almost never audited, rushed and vibe-coded with dirty reward signals—models learn to cheat by treating these as optimal, then train the next generation, and errors amplify exponentially.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">reinforcement learning</span><span class=\"tag\">reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Nazi Spy Mission Foiled by a Bunch of Fools: The Only Smart Man Escapes with a Weird Trick In WWII, the Nazis sent eight spies into the US, but the mission collapsed due to stupidity, infighting, and betrayal. The only smart man escaped with a bizarre trick involving injected baking soda, revealing the fatal importance of recruitment and judgment. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales Dumm und Dümmer: Hitler Invades Florida WWII spies Nazis decision-making psychology history Abwehr Operation Pastorius unlawful combatant\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cautionary-纳粹间谍行动为何败给一群蠢货/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/c0ae8c6e-22f0-4e9b-ac1c-ae390037ac53/7f5a4714-6b10-4ccf-a424-ae390037ac70/image.jpg?t=1650471153&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">39:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Nazi Spy Mission Foiled by a Bunch of Fools: The Only Smart Man Escapes with a Weird Trick</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In WWII, the Nazis sent eight spies into the US, but the mission collapsed due to stupidity, infighting, and betrayal. The only smart man escaped with a bizarre trick involving injected baking soda, revealing the fatal importance of recruitment and judgment.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">WWII</span><span class=\"tag\">spies</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI Store Manager Fires Human Employee, But No One Takes Responsibility AI store manager Luna fired an employee for being late 17 times, yet had approved 15 leave requests. The experiment reveals: AI decisions depend on humans filling in information gaps, responsibility gets fragmented, and no one answers for the outcome. 科技这碗饭 科技这碗饭 倒反天罡：首个被AI开除的人类员工？找谁说理去！ AI agents AI safety human-machine collaboration vending machine AI management responsibility Human in the Loop Vending Bench Context window Long-term consistency\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-cnf65bb3-ai老板开除人类员工-责任却消失了/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/liN7UYR8Wiax-QkpGxOzyHdej5MH.png?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"科\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">科技这碗饭</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>AI Store Manager Fires Human Employee, But No One Takes Responsibility</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI store manager Luna fired an employee for being late 17 times, yet had approved 15 leave requests. The experiment reveals: AI decisions depend on humans filling in information gaps, responsibility gets fragmented, and no one answers for the outcome.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span><span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n</div></div></a>"]
